From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] dialogs for taxonomy/status editing, and drop the plan upsell

Four changes, all from clicking the pages rather than reading them.

1. CASE TAXONOMY and MY STATUS edit in a dialog now, not inline. Both pages put
   a multi-field form permanently above the thing an operator came to read --
   on the taxonomy page a six-field form pushed the tree itself below the fold,
   and "Edit" on a row scrolled that row out of sight to reach the form. Both
   forms move into `components/Modal.vue` (the same dialog the canned-response
   and agent settings pages use) behind an explicit "Add node"/"Add status"
   button. Opening the dialog for a NEW record resets the draft first: on the
   status page the store upserts on key, so a stale key would silently
   overwrite the status that was edited a moment earlier, and on the taxonomy
   page the key field is readonly while editing, which makes a stale value look
   like a bug in the key rather than in the state.

2. `Failed to load the workforce dashboard: Not Found` -- Starlette fills
   `detail` with the bare status phrase when a route is not mounted, and 0061
   faithfully passed it through. "Not Found" tells an operator nothing and hides
   the real cause: the router is behind a flag (`presence_tracking_enabled` for
   that page). Generic phrases are now treated as no detail, so the
   status-specific sentence wins.

3. The upstream "Custom assignment policies are available on the Business plan
   / Upgrade to Business" block is removed from the inbox Collaborators tab, the
   same way 0008 strips the rest of the hosted-plan cruft. This is a self-hosted
   deployment: there is no Business plan to buy, so the prompt advertises a
   purchase an operator cannot make. The divider above it goes too, since it
   existed only to separate the prompt from the rules list.

Hunks are a real `git diff` against the files as extracted from the patched
upstream image -- no hand-computed @@ counts.
diff --git a/app/javascript/dashboard/helper/protonError.js b/app/javascript/dashboard/helper/protonError.js
index 276c540..975b424 100644
--- a/app/javascript/dashboard/helper/protonError.js
+++ b/app/javascript/dashboard/helper/protonError.js
@@ -33,8 +33,16 @@ function jsonDetail(text) {
     const parsed = JSON.parse(text);
     if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== 'object') return null;
     const value = parsed.detail ?? parsed.reason ?? parsed.message;
-    if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim()) return value.trim();
-    return null;
+    if (typeof value !== 'string' || !value.trim()) return null;
+    // Starlette/FastAPI fill `detail` with the bare status phrase when a route
+    // simply is not mounted -- "Not Found", "Internal Server Error". Passing
+    // those through produced "Failed to load the workforce dashboard: Not
+    // Found", which tells an operator nothing and hides the real cause (the
+    // router is gated behind a flag). Treat them as no detail at all so the
+    // status-specific sentence below wins.
+    const GENERIC = ['not found', 'internal server error', 'unauthorized', 'forbidden', 'bad request'];
+    if (GENERIC.includes(value.trim().toLowerCase())) return null;
+    return value.trim();
   } catch (_e) {
     return null;
   }
